Improving Speech-to-Text Accuracy with GitHub Copilot

This document provides a comprehensive set of instructions, prompts, and code comments that can be added to your GitHub repository to guide Copilot toward improving your Speech-to-Text (STT) system's accuracy. These suggestions address issues such as repeated words, hallucinated (extra) words, and incorrect transcriptions.


A) Audio Front-End (Noise & Gain)

// TASK: Improve STT accuracy by fixing the audio front-end.
// Requirements:
// - Force mono 16 kHz PCM, 16-bit, little-endian.
// - Add denoise and AGC with conservative settings (avoid clipping).
// - Hard-limit peak to -3 dBFS and normalize RMS to ~-20 dBFS.
// - Reject chunks where clipping_ratio > 1% or SNR < 10 dB.
// - Unit test: verify resampler, channel downmix, and peak/RMS stats.


B) Voice Activity Detection (VAD) + Endpointing

// TASK: Add robust VAD + endpointing for streaming ASR.
// Implement WebRTC VAD (aggressiveness 2–3) OR Silero VAD.
// Emit "segment start" on speech onset; "segment end" after 300–500 ms of silence.
// Parameters: min_speech_ms=200, min_silence_ms=300, max_segment_ms=15000.
// Only send audio to ASR while "in speech" to reduce hallucinations.
// Include jitter buffer (±100 ms) to avoid word truncation at edges.


C) Chunking & Overlap Logic (Prevents Repeats)

// TASK: Rework chunker to use fixed windows with controlled overlap.
// Use window=20s, hop=5s for batch; for streaming use 1–2s frames with 0.5s overlap.
// Maintain rolling "emitted_tokens" and do n-gram dedup across overlap boundaries.
// Only accept new tokens whose char range does NOT fully overlap previously emitted timestamps.


D) Decoder Configuration (Whisper / Faster-Whisper Examples)

// TASK: Configure Whisper to reduce repetitions and hallucinations.
// - temperature: start at 0.0, enable temperature cycling up to 0.5 on failure
// - beam_size: 5–10 (or best_of=5 for greedy variants)
// - condition_on_previous_text: false
// - no_speech_threshold: 0.6
// - logprob_threshold: -1.0
// - compression_ratio_threshold: 2.4
// - suppress_tokens: [-1] plus built-in list
// - language: set explicitly when known
// - initial_prompt: domain keywords
// - vad_filter: true with vad_parameters(min_silence_duration_ms=300)
// - word_timestamps: true


E) Interim vs. Final Results (Debounce + Stability)

// TASK: Implement a stability gate for partial transcripts.
// Keep a rolling buffer of partial tokens with timestamps+logprobs.
// Only emit to UI if either:
//   a) token is older than 1.0s and unchanged for 2 consecutive frames, or
//   b) segment closed by VAD.
// Debounce UI updates to 100–250 ms to avoid flicker and early repeats.


F) Post-Processing Guards (Safe De-dup + Confidence Filter)

// TASK: Add post-processing to reduce repeats and extras.
// - Remove immediate duplicate n-grams up to n=3.
// - Drop trailing filler words if avg_logprob < -1.2 or confidence < 0.6.
// - If two adjacent words overlap >70% in timestamps, keep the higher-confidence one.
// - Preserve punctuation and casing.
// - Add language-specific contraction and numeral rules.


G) Domain & Punctuation Models

// TASK: Add lightweight punctuation + capitalization model post-ASR.
// Add domain lexicon for biasing via initial_prompt or hotwords.
// Provide hooks to update the lexicon at runtime.


H) Testing & Metrics

// TASK: Add an evaluation harness for ASR:
// - Build gold dataset (10–30 clips) representing your environment.
// - Compute WER, CER, and repetitions per minute (RPM).
// - Log avg token logprob and extra-word rate.
// - Add regression tests to fail if WER or RPM worsen by >10%.
// - Save per-segment JSON logs.


I) Logging & Observability

// TASK: Add debug hooks:
// - Print decoder params per segment.
// - Plot VAD states with timestamps.
// - Emit diff between interim/final transcripts.
// - Redact PII in logs.


Minimal Config Example (Faster-Whisper)

asr = WhisperModel("medium.en", compute_type="int8_float16")
segments, _ = asr.transcribe(
    audio, 
    beam_size=8,
    temperature=0.0,
    vad_filter=True, 
    vad_parameters=dict(min_silence_duration_ms=300),
    condition_on_previous_text=False,
    word_timestamps=True,
    no_speech_threshold=0.6,
    log_prob_threshold=-1.0,
    compression_ratio_threshold=2.4,
    initial_prompt="Product names: Recipeh, Kafka, ZMK; tech terms: Kubernetes, Kafka, S3."
)


Overlap-Aware De-dup (Pseudo)

def emit_new_words(words, already_emitted, iou_thresh=0.7):
    out = []
    for w in words:
        if not overlaps_mostly(w, already_emitted, iou_thresh):
            out.append(w)
            already_emitted.add(w)
    return out


